		<content type="html" xml:base="http://localhost/opengd77/viewtopic.php?t=5060&amp;p=36753#p36753"><![CDATA[
Hello,<br>i own 1 Motorola DM4601, 2 Motorola DP3401, 1 Hytera G36. Then 1 Baofeng DM-1701, 1 Retevis RT-3S and 1 TYT MD-9600, with OpenGD77 installed.<br>With Motorola and Hytera radios, no problem to hang up my Pi-Star dual hat Hotspot, BER around 05-06%<br>With Baofeng and Retevis, no problem too, BER around 01-02%. Difference is a matter of frequency tuning in hotspot.<br>With TYT, i loose 50% of attempt to link my hotspot, with variable BER. Also BER is surprisingly high catching some repeater with full scale signal, but not all.<br>I finished ideas to how to fix it.<p>Statistics: Posted by <a href="http://localhost/opengd77/memberlist.php?mode=viewprofile&amp;u=558">IK1HJT</a> — Mon Apr 14, 2025 7:26 pm</p><hr />
]]></content>
